{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Elam.</b> This prophecy concerns the coming of Nebuchadnezzar. The sense of Elam: even Elam, over whom Nebuchadnezzar had prevailed, he will take up the quiver and come against Jerusalem." "<b>And Kir.</b> For even though they are masters of the lands of Kir, as in \"and I summoned from Kir\" (Amos 9:7), he will uncover his shields against Israel around Jerusalem."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:35.900995988Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}